   "notes": "Montagu House (Sidney Sussex College, 1930s neo-Georgian), corner face to Sidney St/Sussex St: deep red brick with banded/rusticated brick corner piers, a stone frontispiece bay (x~4) with stone balcony at second floor and carved college arms in a broken pediment, arched multi-pane sash on the first floor of the other bay, heavy black timber eaves cornice and slate mansard with pedimented dormers above. Stone ground-floor surround with 'MONTAGU HOUSE' incised in the frieze; shop was Costa in the photo, fascia_text from current OSM POI (Ecco, 25) is a guess."
